    "user_request_original": "Design a 36-layer planar dielectric filter on fused silica substrate with air incidence at 0 degrees unpolarized illumination. Stack topology: Air | Ta2O5 | SiO2 | Ta2O5 | SiO2 | ... alternating for 18 pairs (36 finite layers total) | Fused Silica. Materials: Ta2O5 (high index) and SiO2 (low index). Optimize all 36 layer thicknesses as continuous variables bounded in [15, 355] nm. Implement hard projection operator that clamps any optimizer-proposed thickness to this range before TMM evaluation. Add matrix condition number diagnostic: if cond(M) > 1e10 during TMM solve, halt scoring and return warning. Objectives: maximize mean transmittance in 420-700nm band, minimize mean transmittance at 355nm single wavelength, minimize mean transmittance in 355-365nm band, minimize mean transmittance in 1030-1080nm band. Spectral grid: 1nm spacing from 350-1100nm. Initialize with quarter-wave thicknesses at 355nm (Ta2O5: ~62nm, SiO2: ~95nm) with 10% random perturbation. Use gradient-based thickness optimizer with 500 iterations maximum. Topology realization override: disregard any symbolic repeat count, range, or ellipsis above and use exactly 6 alternating Ta2O5/SiO2 pairs (12 finite layers). Optimize only continuous physical thicknesses; the task compiler must fully expand every finite layer. Canonical user controls: incidence angles 0 degrees. polarization unpolarized. wavelength intervals 355-355 nm, 355-365 nm, 420-700 nm, 1030-1080 nm. soft objectives: high average transmittance in 420-700 nm; low average transmittance at 355 nm; low average transmittance in 355-365 nm; low average transmittance in 1030-1080 nm. behaviors to suppress or avoid: high transmittance at 355 nm; high transmittance in 355-365 nm; high transmittance in 1030-1080 nm; high loss in 420-700 nm. manufacturing constraints: maximum 36 layers; layer thickness range 20-350 nm.",
    "normalized_request_english": "Design a 12-layer alternating Ta2O5/SiO2 dielectric filter on fused silica, illuminated at 0 degrees unpolarized. Optimize all 12 layer thicknesses continuously within [20, 350] nm. Maximize mean transmittance in 420-700 nm. Minimize mean transmittance at 355 nm, in 355-365 nm, and in 1030-1080 nm. Sweep 350-1100 nm at 1 nm spacing.",
